    "status": "present",
    "value": "Find the smallest index containing target in a mountain array using only its length/get API and at most100 get calls. The approach is: cache API reads; binary-search peak, increasing half first, then decreasing half. Its target cost is O(log n) API calls/time/cache; fewer than100 gets at n<=10000. Treat the invariant underlying that approach as the reason each local update preserves the required result. Check it against an independent bounded reference before relying on large-domain constructions."
  },
